From 026df62b1453812b89166ac0ef1a95f1ce66b34a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:46:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: Make OpenScanner a request, report a type of our
 own, settle driver ties

OpenScanner can take longer than D-Bus's default call timeout on a
network scanner (16 and 25 s through airscan), so it is a request now:
the call returns at once and the Response carries session_handle, or
error (busy or failed) and message. Closing the request gives no
Response and lets the scanner go.

The type in the scanner info is the portal's word for the device,
scanner, film, camera or virtual, and not the driver's own string,
which differs between drivers and can hold an address.

Driver order no longer depends on which driver answered first: ties go
by name, and an entry of scanner-devices.json can name the driver that
opens the scanner first. A second driver is tried only after one that
says it does not drive the scanner (INVAL or UNSUPPORTED), not after a
busy scanner or an I/O error, since a driver that failed half way may
have left the device in a state a second one resets. The scanner info
names the driver that will open it, also in the answer to
SelectScanners.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
